            <ArticleTitle>[Diagnostic image (243). A woman with an epigastric mass and vomiting].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1739</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 87-year-old woman presented with epigastric pain and vomiting. Abdominal examination revealed an epigastric mass of 10 by 15 cm. Computed tomography of the abdomen demonstrated protrusion of peritoneal contents through a large defect in the linea alba.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
